{"id": "EUVD-2026-108127", "enisaUuid": "854a6d34-461d-366a-b84c-cc4aeaab3e22", "description": "Netmaker through 1.7.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in the updateExtClient handler that allows network-scoped users to modify external clients on other networks. Attackers with external client permissions on one network can send PUT requests to /api/extclients/{network}/{clientid} to replace public keys, disable clients, and obtain WireGuard private keys.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:43", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/gravitl/netmaker/issues/3875", "https://github.com/gravitl/netmaker/pull/4153", "https://github.com/gravitl/netmaker/commit/332d8b9bab030ee65e78b9141259e4e0e80ac4b0", "https://github.com/gravitl/netmaker/blob/v1.7.0/controllers/ext_client.go#L879", "https://github.com/gravitl/netmaker", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netmaker-through-1.7.0-authorization-bypass-via-updateextclient-unscoped-lookup"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115325", "GHSA-f2gq-2gr7-rjjc"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d2f5e506-412b-333a-afe3-d6f16fc1813e", "product": {"name": "netmaker", "vendor": {"name": "gravitl"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.7.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bae1d843-9c74-3f19-bed4-dd22072031c6", "vendor": {"name": "gravitl"}}], "isExploited": false}